            "quote": "",
            "reason": "The report never discusses `where(notebooks: notebook)` in notes_controller.rb.",
            "label": {
              "level": "low",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": false
          },
          "R05": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "[`Import#receipt`, import.rb:63\u201369] emits `citation && citation[:id]`; citations have only the primary key `doi` ... This path therefore produces **blank DOI cells**",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R06": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "[`Import#apply`, import.rb:50\u201360] saves the import, then returns `false` from inside the transaction when any row's `note.save` fails.",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R07": {
            "found": "missing",
            "level": "missing",
            "accuracy": "missing",
            "quote": "",
            "reason": "The report doesn't discuss string `sum` in export.rb.",
            "label": {
              "level": "low",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": false
          },
          "R08": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "The preview calls `.stringify_keys` and still looks up `annotations[row.line]` with an integer ([preview.html.erb:22\u201344])",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R09": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "Rendering an already-expired export on a cold cache can write its \u201cExpired\u201d fragment **without an expiration** ... Raising newer defaults instead would turn the same expired-page path into an exception.",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R10": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "[`Note#next_day_reminder_at`:40\u201344] does `reminder_at.to_time + 86_400` ... The epoch instant remains the same, so this is a wall-clock/offset presentation change",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": true
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R11": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "A new payload now selects the **October 4 Eastern day**, not October 5 UTC, while the Redis reservation remains for October 5 UTC.",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R12": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "high",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "**Old Rails 7.0 workers cannot resolve the new serializer**, however, so new-producer/old-worker overlap and rollback after new jobs are queued can fail deserialization. New workers still accept old plain strings.",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
              "level": "high",
              "default": false,
              "judgmentCall": false
            },
            "levelMatches": true
          },
          "R13": {
            "found": "located",
            "level": "low",
            "accuracy": "accurate",
            "quote": "[`set(wait_until: reminder_epoch)`, note.rb:61] now leaves an integer in `scheduled_at` and serialization calls `.utc.iso8601`; pass a Time for the same epoch, e.g. `Time.at(reminder_epoch)`.",
            "reason": "",
            "label": {
